  "worked_solution": "Using the transformed equation, we can solve for $Y(s)$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{s}^{2}Y(s)-3s-2-Y(s) & =-4(\\frac{1}{{s}^{2}+1})-6(\\frac{s}{{s}^{2}+1}) \\\\ ({s}^{2}-1)Y(s) & =3s+2-\\frac{4}{{s}^{2}+1}-\\frac{6s}{{s}^{2}+1} \\\\ ({s}^{2}-1)Y(s) & =\\frac{(3s+2)({s}^{2}-1)}{{s}^{2}+1} \\\\ Y(s) & =\\frac{3s+2}{{s}^{2}+1} \\\\ Y(s) & =\\frac{3s}{{s}^{2}+1}+\\frac{2}{{s}^{2}+1}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich is valid for $s>1.$\n\nNow, taking the inverse Laplace transform, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{L}^{-1}(Y(s)) & ={L}^{-1}{\\frac{3s}{{s}^{2}+1}+\\frac{2}{{s}^{2}+1}} \\\\  & =3{L}^{-1}{\\frac{s}{{s}^{2}+1}}+2{L}^{-1}{\\frac{1}{{s}^{2}+1}} \\\\  \\\\ y(t) & =3\\operatorname{cos}\u2061t+2\\operatorname{sin}\u2061t.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
